{
  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_013: multimodal, scgpt+resnet50, avgpool, concat → 51.2% acc), the most fundamental uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion is actually contributing value over a single modality. config_022 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) uses the identical RNA encoder (scgpt) and aggregation (avgpool) as config_013, differing only in the absence of the image branch. This makes it a clean single-variable comparison that isolates the contribution of the image modality. If RNA alone matches or exceeds 51.2%, it signals that the current image encoder/fusion is not adding signal and we should pivot to improving the RNA representation or trying a stronger image encoder. If RNA alone is substantially lower, it confirms the image modality is contributing and justifies further multimodal exploration. Under a limited budget, establishing this baseline before testing more complex fusion/aggregation variants is the highest-information-per-experiment choice."
}

